      53.04,
      542.51,
      120.74
    ],
    "text": "assessment of the evidence, the identification of the land and the application of the Act. The written submissions develop those objections but do not explain why they called for revisionary interference. The assertion of grave and irreparable loss appears in support of the application for an interim stay.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Light"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.960000038146973
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      72.02,
      140.06,
      542.98,
      262.46
    ],
    "text": "The complaint that the High Court dismissed the revision application without issuing notice does not, of itself, establish an error. The High Court was entitled to decline notice if the material placed before it disclosed no exceptional circumstance warranting interference. The matters urged here do not establish that the learned Magistrate applied an impermissible test or that the High Court overlooked a subsisting written authority within section 9 of the Act. I therefore find no basis to disturb the judgment of the High Court.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Light"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.960000038146973
    ]
